cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rigorous-levels, cite it as below. Nothing here is a third-party or accredited certification: a guaranteed interval follows from the proof in docs/PROOF.md and from the correctness of Arb/FLINT."
title: "rigorous-levels: guaranteed eigenvalue intervals for the charge-basis rotor, the spherical rotor, the 1Σ molecule, the Mathieu characteristic values and the fluxonium, with a sandboxed multiport for external solvers"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-12"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24172688
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24172688
    description: "Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest version"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24172689
    description: "Version 0.3.0"
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Locatelli
    given-names: Roberto
repository-code: "https://github.com/robertolocatelli81-dev/rigorous-levels"
abstract: "Mathematically guaranteed intervals [low, high] containing the exact eigenvalues of the written Hamiltonian, with the truncation of the basis included in the proof (Rayleigh–Ritz above; Young's inequality and Gershgorin bounds on the truncated block below; eigenvalue counts by Sylvester's law of inertia in Arb ball arithmetic). A convergence warning for scqubits with a declared threshold rule, a multiport that runs other people's solvers in a fail-closed isolation engine and compares them with the intervals, and the guaranteed per-level error of the Duffing model."
keywords:
  - verified numerics
  - eigenvalue enclosures
  - transmon
  - fluxonium
  - Mathieu functions
  - polar molecules
  - ball arithmetic
